-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_strings_err_unknown_escape_char.pcpp - break step of lex_strings.pcpp:
  an escape C++ does not know in a character literal (PR0064, a warning:
  the character is the q)

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lex_strings_err_unknown_escape_char.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\lex_strings_err_unknown_escape_char.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  The marked line reports that warning, once (the build reports nothing
  more about it), then the program prints:
  EXPECT:
    q
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_strings_err_unknown_escape_char;

begin
  println("{}", '\q'); // WARN PR0064@17: character literal: unknown escape sequence '\q'
end.
